    description: "py.py and jupyter.py use Python's ast module, not TreeSitterAnalyzer.\nThey won't get automatic Tier 1 annotation. Need a dedicated integration\npoint — either an ast-module-aware variant of classify_access, or a\npost-hoc pass that maps ast node types to the same access_mode vocabulary.\n\nPython is the highest-value language for dataflow analysis: module-level\nglobals (test isolation), framework state (Django settings, Flask config),\nand the PlazaFlow Yjs patterns all involve Python.\n\nDepends on: core dataflow YAMLs (Python patterns defined).\nSee ADR-0015 §5 coverage gap table."  # a7f1
    fields: {}  # a7f1
